From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Complete control frames without monopolizing the native event loop

Assemble stream replies across short reads and interruptions. A partial EOF
remains an error, socket errors survive, and descriptor zero remains valid.
Queue control output through libubox ustream instead of spinning on EAGAIN on
an accepted nonblocking socket. Retain the single native client owner and its
existing inactivity timeout, closing only after output drains or fails.

Bound one level-triggered conntrack event turn to 32 datagrams so continuous
events cannot indefinitely exclude queued shutdown signals and control I/O.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
